# Old Tradenet 2.0 DCCA exports used as byte-for-byte oracles for DccaWorkbookWriter.
#
# The files themselves are NOT committed: they hold real company names and voucher numbers. Point
# TRADENET_DCCA_LEGACY_XLSX at one or more of them (';'-separated) to run
# AccountSummaryDccaExportTests.Replaying_a_legacy_export_reproduces_every_part_byte_for_byte,
# which parses each file's own data rows, feeds them back through the writer, and requires all ten
# OOXML parts to be SHA-256-identical.
#
# This manifest is the test's guard against verifying the WRONG file. Our own output would pass a
# self-comparison trivially, so a path whose hash is not listed here fails loudly instead of
# quietly "passing". Add an entry only after confirming the file really was produced by the old
# system: 10 zip entries with sharedStrings.xml last, worksheet named Sheet1,
# cellXfs count="4", and non-1980 zip timestamps (our writer pins 1980-01-01).
#
# <sha256 of the .xlsx>  <data rows>  <provenance>
ffd803d5f5ac747b076cabbe1a7e30f204ad4b65a9f638bb45480fdaee439ca4  543  TradenetAdmin/uploads/AccountSummary.xlsx at origin/master, generated 2 Sep 2021
3f33778a7ae2ae5cd542de53ff244f549962c5f56084143d0e5aafd45ba20340  138  customer-supplied old-system export, generated 17 Jun 2026 (zip stamps 2026-06-17 09:35)
